.TH MULTI-SETTINGS 1 "September 2026" "Onboarding 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
multi-settings \- manage Ubuntu accounts, YubiKeys, and system hardening
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B multi-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B multi-settings
starts the native GTK 4 Onboarding application.
It can create and remove local standard users, enroll YubiKeys, configure
password plus YubiKey authentication, and independently audit or apply DevSec
OS and SSH hardening. Results can be saved as CSV.
.PP
The graphical application runs as the current user. Operations that modify
the system are delegated to a PolicyKit-authorized helper.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/multi-settings/custom-settings.yaml
Automatically loaded user settings that override bundled settings and the
hardening role defaults.
.TP
.I /usr/share/multi-settings/custom-settings.yaml
Optional settings injected while building the package manually.
.TP
.I /var/lib/multi-settings
Protected application state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
